1
00:00:32,609 --> 00:00:36,814
But hey, if that gets on my clothes...

2
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,588
School is peaceful.

3
00:00:51,410 --> 00:00:54,803
As if nothing ever happened.

4
00:00:57,307 --> 00:01:00,721
Are you crazy? Are you crazy? Are you crazy?

5
00:01:00,721 --> 00:01:03,355
What is wrong with you?

6
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:06,385
Why won't you ever listen? Seriously!

7
00:01:06,385 --> 00:01:09,639
Mom and Dad, too.

8
00:01:09,639 --> 00:01:12,281
Jung Yeon.

9
00:01:12,281 --> 00:01:13,334
Everyone's the same.

10
00:01:13,334 --> 00:01:15,679
Are you okay? Are you all right?

11
00:01:15,679 --> 00:01:17,554
Oh my. What do I do?

12
00:01:17,554 --> 00:01:19,454
Seriously.

13
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:23,959
Honestly, Kim Ha Yeon! Really. Seriously.

14
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:25,362
Let's go now.

15
00:01:25,362 --> 00:01:27,642
Jung Yeon.

16
00:01:27,642 --> 00:01:29,316
Oh, no.

17
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:45,272
Go, Ha Yeon. Go on ahead.

18
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:46,773
Damn it.

19
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,706
Ha Yeon, go!

20
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,589
But subtly,

21
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:57,006
so very subtly.

22
00:01:58,869 --> 00:02:04,041
Sorry, what is it? What?
Let me look. Just show me once.

23
00:02:04,041 --> 00:02:07,628
No. No. I said no.

24
00:02:09,989 --> 00:02:10,989
Sorry.

25
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:13,105
I'm really sorry.

26
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:15,099
Seriously.

27
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,453
Sorry.

28
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:21,584
- I really...
- Doesn't matter. Follow me.

29
00:02:21,584 --> 00:02:24,570
- What's the harm in showing me once?
- I said no.

30
00:02:24,570 --> 00:02:26,070
What? Sung Sae Ryeong?

31
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:30,626
Right. So what happened exactly?
Come on, tell us the story.

32
00:02:30,626 --> 00:02:33,042
You know that transfer student from Seoul?

33
00:02:33,042 --> 00:02:35,670
She fought Sung Sae Ryeong over Cho Yu Gyeom.

34
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:37,532
No way. Is that true?

35
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:39,534
But Sung Sae Ryeong got beaten to a pulp.

36
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:44,710
That Seoul bitch is scary.
I heard she was taken to the hospital.

37
00:02:45,317 --> 00:02:48,670
But you know Sung Sae Ryeong's family?

38
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:52,710
She got hurt that badly,
so isn't it weird that they're so quiet?

39
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:57,135
Exactly. Normally they'd be raising hell
by now, wouldn't they?

40
00:02:57,135 --> 00:03:00,347
Maybe the Seoul girl's family isn't ordinary.

41
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:02,641
What does her family do, anyway?

42
00:03:02,641 --> 00:03:04,302
How would I know?

43
00:03:04,302 --> 00:03:07,599
It's a horror. This school is a horror.

44
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:12,119
What? Was someone in there?

45
00:03:12,119 --> 00:03:13,670
It's not Sung Sae Ryeong, is it?

46
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:17,196
Run! Hurry! Go, go!

47
00:03:25,670 --> 00:03:28,395
A tiny crack within it

48
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:33,630
began to seep into our time.

49
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,650
[4. A New World]

50
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:39,845
[Episode 4]

51
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:41,433
Raise your head.

52
00:03:48,979 --> 00:03:53,938
Jae Jin, you must live an upright life.

53
00:03:53,938 --> 00:03:55,392
Yes, Father.

54
00:03:56,903 --> 00:04:00,240
I hear Yu Gyeom was going out with a girl,

55
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:04,643
then strayed to another girl,
and that's how this mess began.

56
00:04:04,643 --> 00:04:08,540
Isn't this what you did 18 years ago?

57
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:13,372
It's because you're that kind of man
that Yu Gyeom did such a thing!

58
00:04:14,456 --> 00:04:16,220
I'm sorry, Father.

59
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:22,922
Why is Yu Gyeom's mother standing there?
Didn't I say to fetch Sae Ryeong's grandmother?

60
00:04:22,922 --> 00:04:24,413
Yes, Father.

61
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,514
Oh, my.

62
00:04:31,563 --> 00:04:34,231
Sorry, sorry.

63
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:40,363
No. Please, no. Ma'am,

64
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:44,138
You have nothing to be sorry for.

65
00:04:44,138 --> 00:04:47,197
I'm the one who should apologize.

66
00:04:47,197 --> 00:04:51,401
My child hurt your precious granddaughter...

67
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:57,309
Please, just take this for now.

68
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:04,458
Ma'am, this isn't a matter of
whether you accept it or not.

69
00:05:04,458 --> 00:05:07,599
It's only right that we give it to you.

70
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:12,650
Sae Ryeong got hurt
because of our child, after all.

71
00:05:12,650 --> 00:05:14,272
Here.

72
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:18,277
It's fine. I don't need to take it.

73
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,804
What is she saying?

74
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:26,292
Um...

75
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:31,994
You... Didn't you say
you're taking sign language?

76
00:05:31,994 --> 00:05:33,652
This is sign language.

77
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:38,619
Hold on.

78
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:49,099
I can't write. I don't know Hangul.

79
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:56,417
Ma'am, even so, this is...

80
00:05:56,417 --> 00:06:00,617
something you really must accept.

81
00:06:02,709 --> 00:06:07,417
No, it's fine. You paid the hospital bill.
That's a lot of money, too.

82
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:18,109
She says paying the hospital bill is enough.
That was a lot of money, too.

83
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:25,511
Excuse me. Tell her we can't do that.

84
00:06:25,511 --> 00:06:30,033
It's only right that we give her this money.

85
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:45,314
She says thank you, but just take it back.

86
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:59,169
Sae Ryeong, let's go.

87
00:06:59,169 --> 00:07:01,023
No. You guys go ahead.

88
00:07:02,464 --> 00:07:04,341
Cho Yu Gyeom?

89
00:07:04,341 --> 00:07:06,497
Fine, let's go.

90
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:14,311
Hey...

91
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,495
Is your head all right?

92
00:07:22,133 --> 00:07:24,706
I didn't mean to. I'm sorry.

93
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:27,731
Get lost.

94
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:37,882
Let's go.

95
00:07:37,882 --> 00:07:41,524
Sung Sae Ryeong, time to go home.
You can't, can you?

96
00:07:41,524 --> 00:07:44,459
Dummy, dummy.

97
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:49,503
Well, well, Cho Yu Gyeom.

98
00:07:49,503 --> 00:07:51,153
Did you see that earlier?

99
00:07:51,153 --> 00:07:54,469
How Goh Hui Jun made a real fool of himself?

100
00:07:54,469 --> 00:07:56,709
You told me to!

101
00:07:56,709 --> 00:07:57,769
Let's go.

102
00:07:57,769 --> 00:07:59,782
Sung Sae Ryeong's not here yet.

103
00:07:59,782 --> 00:08:01,666
Sae Ryeong!

104
00:08:01,666 --> 00:08:03,060
You don't need to call her.

105
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,609
Why not? Hey!

106
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,066
We broke up.

107
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:09,825
What?

108
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:14,878
I said Sung Sae Ryeong and I broke up.

109
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,622
If you're not coming, I'm going ahead.

110
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,562
Cho Yu Gyeom!

111
00:08:19,562 --> 00:08:22,044
Give me more details!

112
00:08:22,044 --> 00:08:24,283
What are you talking about?

113
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:31,970
- Did they really break up?
- I heard they really did.

114
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,167
Really?

115
00:08:34,167 --> 00:08:35,209
Stop it.

116
00:08:35,209 --> 00:08:37,542
That means it's really over, right?

117
00:08:37,542 --> 00:08:39,859
Here you go, ma'am.

118
00:08:39,859 --> 00:08:44,351
Ma'am, if your granddaughter's wound
gets worse or anything...

119
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:50,026
Yes, I'm so sorry.

120
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:52,991
Thank you.

121
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:54,368
Let's go.

122
00:08:59,204 --> 00:09:04,730
You said you were taking a sign language class,
so I thought you'd be good at it.

123
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:05,920
What was that?

124
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,819
Will that get you a good grade?

125
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:10,249
I'd probably still get an A.

126
00:09:10,249 --> 00:09:11,718
Oh, my!

127
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:14,120
What do you mean, an A?

128
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,276
You should be getting an A+.

129
00:09:17,850 --> 00:09:19,142
Mom.

130
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:21,000
What is it?

131
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,378
You go on ahead.

132
00:09:22,378 --> 00:09:24,094
What? Why?

133
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:30,089
Hey, Sae Ryeong and Yu Gyeom broke up!

134
00:09:30,089 --> 00:09:31,760
Don't be ridiculous.

135
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:33,360
Yu Gyeom told me himself.

136
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,584
Me too. I heard it too.

137
00:09:34,584 --> 00:09:37,661
He just came right out and said it.
They broke up.

138
00:09:37,661 --> 00:09:38,949
Crazy!

139
00:09:38,949 --> 00:09:40,712
That's crazy.

140
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:29,520
You didn't, did you?
You didn't really break up, right?

141
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,160
Come on, it makes no sense. It's all BS.

142
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:35,271
Right? You just had a fight, right?

143
00:10:35,271 --> 00:10:37,861
Yeah. Fighting is part of growing up.

144
00:10:37,861 --> 00:10:40,181
Hey, you...

145
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:43,759
Sae Ryeong got beaten up by that Seoul girl
and was hospitalized.

146
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:46,187
You really can't dump her.

147
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:49,460
Hey, Cho Yu Gyeom! I'm serious!

148
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:51,318
You didn't really break up, right?

149
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:54,153
Won Bae, I told you, it's all a lie.

150
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:56,906
Why would Yu Gyeom dump a girl like Sae Ryeong?

151
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,856
Not unless he's really lost his mind.

152
00:11:00,564 --> 00:11:01,851
Goh Hui Jun.

153
00:11:01,851 --> 00:11:02,864
Yeah?

154
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:05,525
I've lost my mind.

155
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:10,461
I've really lost it.

156
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:11,797
Let me out.

157
00:11:14,299 --> 00:11:17,677
What's he saying? Why's he getting off?

158
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:19,214
I'll go ahead.

159
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:25,430
Guys?

160
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:29,272
What's with him?
They didn't really break up, did they?

161
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:32,000
Didn't he just say he lost his mind?

162
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,777
Wait, isn't this Upo Country Club?

163
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:38,587
Whoa! He's going to see that Seoul girl.
She lives here, right?

164
00:11:38,587 --> 00:11:40,650
Hey, wait.

165
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:45,125
You're really out of your mind. Go on, go!

166
00:11:58,107 --> 00:11:59,311
Excuse me.

167
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,706
I wanted to ask you something.

168
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,397
I'm not a bad person.

169
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:13,403
No, that's not it.

170
00:12:15,044 --> 00:12:19,716
By any chance, that sign language thing...

171
00:12:19,716 --> 00:12:21,325
Do you tutor it, too?

172
00:12:21,325 --> 00:12:22,353
Sign language?

173
00:12:22,353 --> 00:12:23,452
Yes.

174
00:12:23,452 --> 00:12:26,094
I'm a college student,
and I'd like to learn it.

175
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:36,176
Well, you can just memorize sign language
from books or videos, so--

176
00:12:36,176 --> 00:12:38,675
No, I mean signing as fast as you do.

177
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:40,009
What?

178
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,764
When you sign that fast, I can't follow at all.

179
00:12:42,764 --> 00:12:44,009
So...

180
00:12:45,704 --> 00:12:49,369
Then you could ask to slow it down--

181
00:12:49,369 --> 00:12:50,947
Do you have a phone?

182
00:12:53,044 --> 00:12:54,665
You do.

183
00:12:54,665 --> 00:12:56,092
010...

184
00:12:57,486 --> 00:12:59,696
- Could you type it in?
- Okay.

185
00:12:59,696 --> 00:13:03,370
010-0711-9012.

186
00:13:03,370 --> 00:13:05,076
That's my number.

187
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:10,190
Once or twice a week. Think of it as
teaching English conversation.

188
00:13:10,190 --> 00:13:13,657
For the fee, how about 20,000 won an hour?

189
00:13:13,657 --> 00:13:16,232
Any time works, just not too early.

190
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:19,396
Let me know if you're interested.

191
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:21,540
Well, then.

192
00:13:33,244 --> 00:13:37,083
Miss, Madam's asking what's going on.

193
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:38,825
It's nothing.

194
00:14:46,884 --> 00:14:49,015
How did you break up?

195
00:14:50,224 --> 00:14:54,651
You said you were scared
of breaking up with Sung Sae Ryeong.

196
00:14:55,584 --> 00:15:00,829
I was afraid that if I broke up with
Sae Ryeong, something would happen to her.

197
00:15:00,829 --> 00:15:02,821
That really scared me.

198
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:07,652
But this time, I realized.

199
00:15:10,911 --> 00:15:12,467
Sae Ryeong, what...

200
00:15:13,914 --> 00:15:15,887
Did she die or something?

201
00:15:18,919 --> 00:15:22,084
I'm not scared of that anymore.

202
00:15:22,084 --> 00:15:27,423
Maybe now I don't even care
what happens to Sae Ryeong.

203
00:15:28,303 --> 00:15:29,999
Yeah.

204
00:15:29,999 --> 00:15:31,725
I see.

205
00:15:32,850 --> 00:15:34,994
So I was able to break up.

206
00:15:40,944 --> 00:15:43,012
You know, Ha Yeon, that day...

207
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:50,281
I got home and opened my bedroom door,
and it smelled really good.

208
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,841
It smelled so good that
I just stayed in my room.

209
00:15:57,499 --> 00:16:00,381
Then my sister called me to eat, so I went out.

210
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:05,792
Even when I was walking outside,
I could still smell it.

211
00:16:08,051 --> 00:16:12,526
So I sniffed around and realized
the smell was coming from my own hand.

212
00:16:23,504 --> 00:16:28,011
Your scent, on the hand that held yours.

213
00:16:32,364 --> 00:16:34,430
I liked that smell so much,

214
00:16:37,184 --> 00:16:38,897
I couldn't even wash my hand.

215
00:16:41,751 --> 00:16:44,129
Come on.

216
00:16:45,918 --> 00:16:47,517
Ha Yeon!

217
00:16:47,517 --> 00:16:48,517
Yeah?

218
00:16:49,176 --> 00:16:52,251
Can I hold your hand?

219
00:17:19,623 --> 00:17:21,874
Really? Is it true?

220
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,620
Won Bae, is it true?

221
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:29,164
I don't know, Your Highness. That bastard
got off without saying a word, right?

222
00:17:29,164 --> 00:17:32,344
Can't you tell? This time it's for real.

223
00:17:33,094 --> 00:17:36,194
But have they ever broken up before?

224
00:17:36,194 --> 00:17:37,848
No, they haven't.

225
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:40,094
Come to think of it, this is the first time.

226
00:17:40,094 --> 00:17:41,494
No way!

227
00:17:41,494 --> 00:17:43,020
That's insane!

228
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,545
Really? For real?

229
00:17:44,545 --> 00:17:45,940
That's crazy.

230
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:48,609
What do you guys keep saying is so crazy?

231
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,744
You mean it's crazy they broke up?

232
00:17:50,744 --> 00:17:52,629
No, that's not what I meant.

233
00:17:52,629 --> 00:17:56,701
Even so, our young master Yu Gyeom
goes straight to see that girl?

234
00:17:56,701 --> 00:17:59,413
They broke up, so he went to see her.

235
00:17:59,413 --> 00:18:02,909
You guys are shocked by everything. Crazy!

236
00:18:03,576 --> 00:18:04,583
So annoying.

237
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:06,501
- Hey.
- What?

238
00:18:07,584 --> 00:18:12,083
Won Bae, so are you coming or not?
We've got nothing to do anyway.

239
00:18:12,083 --> 00:18:15,363
You guys always... You really love this stuff.

240
00:18:15,363 --> 00:18:16,474
Let's go.

241
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:18,597
Not anymore.

242
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:21,685
You going to the arcade, jerk?

243
00:18:21,685 --> 00:18:22,702
Bye.

244
00:18:25,021 --> 00:18:26,355
Jin Mi, what are you doing?

245
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:27,792
What do you think?

246
00:18:27,792 --> 00:18:29,875
They really broke up.

247
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:32,568
So what?

248
00:18:34,158 --> 00:18:37,527
Sung Sae Ryeong and Yu Gyeom are over for good.

249
00:18:58,034 --> 00:19:01,089
Please call me if anything happens.

250
00:19:01,089 --> 00:19:02,600
Ha Yeon's mom.

251
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,876
Ma'am.

252
00:19:12,876 --> 00:19:18,294
With my deepest apologies, I've prepared
this modest meal for you.

253
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:28,833
Either way, because of our boy,
your granddaughter went through so much.

254
00:19:28,833 --> 00:19:31,652
That's why I've invited you here.

255
00:19:37,668 --> 00:19:38,844
Thank you.

256
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:42,792
But you didn't have to do this.

257
00:19:42,792 --> 00:19:45,352
Not at all. This is only right.

258
00:19:45,352 --> 00:19:47,392
This is a token of my sincerity.

259
00:19:47,392 --> 00:19:50,104
Please, eat.

260
00:20:07,583 --> 00:20:10,126
Did Sung Sae Ryeong really break up?

261
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:12,138
Yeah, they say it's for real.

262
00:20:12,138 --> 00:20:14,923
Wrecked. Completely wrecked.

263
00:20:14,923 --> 00:20:16,473
What happened?

264
00:20:47,956 --> 00:20:49,857
Can't resist.

265
00:20:51,334 --> 00:20:52,563
Cheese for me.

266
00:20:53,587 --> 00:20:55,234
Hi.

267
00:20:55,234 --> 00:20:56,924
You're here.

268
00:20:56,924 --> 00:20:58,928
What? Is it for real?

269
00:20:59,551 --> 00:21:01,635
It's real. Why else would I call you?

270
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:05,806
But Sung Sae Ryeong might be testing us,

271
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:08,109
pretending to break up with Cho Yu Gyeom.

272
00:21:08,109 --> 00:21:11,354
If that's the case, we'll look like idiots.

273
00:21:11,354 --> 00:21:15,191
How many years have I been
by Sung Sae Ryeong's side?

274
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:17,485
Four years. Four.

275
00:21:17,485 --> 00:21:22,156
I've watched Sung Sae Ryeong and Cho Yu Gyeom
from the very start until now.

276
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:25,800
They've never broken up, not even as a joke.

277
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:28,157
Least of all from Cho Yu Gyeom.

278
00:21:30,165 --> 00:21:32,545
Do you know what Cho Yu Gyeom said?

279
00:21:33,252 --> 00:21:36,237
"I'm crazy about some other bitch."

280
00:21:38,147 --> 00:21:39,480
So...

281
00:21:40,433 --> 00:21:42,000
what's your point?

282
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,762
Well...

283
00:21:44,762 --> 00:21:49,201
If they broke up, they broke up.
It's not like we can do anything.

284
00:21:49,201 --> 00:21:51,310
Of course we can.

285
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:54,542
Have you forgotten everything
Sung Sae Ryeong did to you?

286
00:21:54,542 --> 00:21:56,395
Lee Na Gyeong, for starters.

287
00:21:57,358 --> 00:22:01,946
Look at her. Just look at her.
You're still like this? Still?

288
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:04,380
And you guys, think about it.

289
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:06,952
Were you okay with Sung Sae Ryeong
going wild every night

290
00:22:06,952 --> 00:22:11,664
and summoning us to the group chat?

291
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:14,705
Nobody even messes with a sleeping dog.

292
00:22:14,705 --> 00:22:18,963
But Sung Sae Ryeong calls us at 2 or 3 a.m.
whenever she likes. And that's not all.

293
00:22:18,963 --> 00:22:22,347
But Kim Jin Mi,
do you really have to go this far?

294
00:22:22,347 --> 00:22:25,553
You were her lackey.

295
00:22:25,553 --> 00:22:27,888
I think you're overstepping.

296
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:31,809
And Sung Sae Ryeong's dad is a lawmaker.

297
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:34,103
Even if she's lost Cho Yu Gyeom's backing.

298
00:22:34,103 --> 00:22:38,065
Right. Sung Sae Ryeong herself is no pushover.

299
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:42,695
Kim Jin Mi, I think you're out of control...

300
00:22:42,695 --> 00:22:45,793
Thinking about Sung Sae Ryeong still scares me.

301
00:22:45,793 --> 00:22:47,210
Don't you feel it too?

302
00:22:47,959 --> 00:22:51,818
You know, I've met kids who are filthy rich,

303
00:22:51,818 --> 00:22:55,647
and kids so poor you'd gasp.

304
00:22:55,647 --> 00:22:59,461
But our dear Sae Ryeong
said she's filthy rich, right?

305
00:22:59,461 --> 00:23:02,083
Right, she did.

306
00:23:02,083 --> 00:23:04,800
So why does she smell like that?

307
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,285
Smell?

308
00:23:06,285 --> 00:23:09,260
What does Sung Sae Ryeong smell like?

309
00:23:15,354 --> 00:23:16,721
A musty smell.

310
00:23:18,065 --> 00:23:20,482
Like a grimy old rag.

311
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:21,818
That mustiness.

312
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:24,695
Strange, isn't it?

313
00:23:24,695 --> 00:23:28,514
Why would a girl that rich smell like that?

314
00:23:28,514 --> 00:23:30,998
And everything she carries is designer.

315
00:23:33,033 --> 00:23:37,666
But you know, in this world,
there are as many fakes as real ones.

316
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:41,514
You mean everything Sung Sae Ryeong
carries is fake?

317
00:23:41,514 --> 00:23:44,372
Have you guys ever seen real designer goods?

318
00:23:45,551 --> 00:23:47,645
I have.

319
00:23:47,645 --> 00:23:49,896
So whose word should you believe?

320
00:23:49,896 --> 00:23:52,640
You saw it. We didn't.

321
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:53,934
Right.

322
00:23:53,934 --> 00:23:56,534
And there's no proof hers are all knockoffs.

323
00:23:56,534 --> 00:23:58,269
Okay.

324
00:23:58,269 --> 00:24:01,195
Then I'll just prove it myself, right?

325
00:24:02,109 --> 00:24:04,414
Can you prove it?

326
00:24:04,414 --> 00:24:07,274
Yeah, it's damn easy.

327
00:24:11,827 --> 00:24:14,140
Sae Ryeong.

328
00:24:15,873 --> 00:24:17,521
What did you do yesterday?

329
00:24:17,521 --> 00:24:18,584
Why?

330
00:24:18,584 --> 00:24:20,709
No, nothing.

331
00:24:20,709 --> 00:24:23,234
Oh, is your head okay now?

332
00:24:23,234 --> 00:24:25,481
Don't worry about it.

333
00:24:28,759 --> 00:24:34,515
But Sae Ryeong, you know...
you didn't break up with Yu Gyeom, did you?

334
00:24:34,515 --> 00:24:37,386
Won Bae said it was just a quick fight. Right?

335
00:24:37,386 --> 00:24:39,561
Why do you want to know?

336
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:43,253
No, I just heard a rumor going around.

337
00:24:43,253 --> 00:24:47,053
You started that rumor, Kim Jin Mi.

338
00:24:47,053 --> 00:24:49,573
What do you mean? Why would I do that?

339
00:24:49,573 --> 00:24:51,573
It wasn't me.

340
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:52,918
Right.

341
00:24:52,918 --> 00:24:55,403
You'd never do that.

342
00:25:05,042 --> 00:25:06,506
Sae Ryeong.

343
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:14,138
- Oh no, what do I do?
- What do I do? What do I do about this?

344
00:25:14,138 --> 00:25:15,472
What is this?

345
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:19,059
What do I do? Guys, what do I do?

346
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:22,855
Shouldn't you take it in
for repairs or something?

347
00:25:22,855 --> 00:25:25,489
Right? Must be.

348
00:25:25,489 --> 00:25:27,197
Forget it. No need to fix it.

349
00:25:27,197 --> 00:25:29,945
No, you have to. You really have to.

350
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:33,198
Sae Ryeong, let's go
to the department store after school.

351
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,559
I'll pay for repairs.

352
00:25:34,559 --> 00:25:37,703
Yeah. There's a department store in Daegu.
Let's go today.

353
00:25:37,703 --> 00:25:40,101
I said forget it.

354
00:25:40,101 --> 00:25:42,792
I bought this abroad,
so it can't be repaired here. Forget it.

355
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:45,419
Sae Ryeong, what are you talking about?

356
00:25:45,419 --> 00:25:49,800
Luxury brands like this get repaired here
even if you bought them abroad.

357
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:52,751
Haven't you heard of a worldwide warranty?

358
00:25:53,762 --> 00:25:57,925
You only buy luxury brands,
and you really didn't know that?

359
00:26:00,462 --> 00:26:02,319
Let's go. Right now. Oh, no!

360
00:26:02,319 --> 00:26:05,022
You guys are coming too, right?

361
00:26:05,022 --> 00:26:07,306
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

362
00:26:07,306 --> 00:26:09,626
I can't today. I'm busy.

363
00:26:09,626 --> 00:26:13,113
Then we can go tomorrow. Right, Sae Ryeong?

364
00:26:13,113 --> 00:26:17,012
The 2811 bus from here takes you
right to the department store.

365
00:26:17,012 --> 00:26:21,402
Sae Ryeong, promise me we'll take this
to the department store tomorrow.

366
00:26:22,612 --> 00:26:24,008
Promise.

367
00:26:49,443 --> 00:26:51,527
Well, well.

368
00:26:51,527 --> 00:26:55,472
Our Yu Gyeom has another great time.

369
00:26:55,472 --> 00:26:59,700
Such a useless, great time.
That's our Yu Gyeom.

370
00:27:01,370 --> 00:27:06,304
I'm tired of doing this every time, too,
so can't you just give up now, sir?

371
00:27:06,304 --> 00:27:08,252
I gave up ages ago.

372
00:27:08,252 --> 00:27:10,714
If a student tells me to give up,
then I give up.

373
00:27:10,714 --> 00:27:15,493
Good job, Jeong Uk. That's it. Bigger strokes.

374
00:27:18,234 --> 00:27:22,119
That was when I was in sixth grade
of elementary school.

375
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:26,562
You know, the year your father
competed in the Olympics.

376
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:31,095
The whole country was in an uproar back then.

377
00:27:31,095 --> 00:27:35,237
Cho Jae Jin placed first in the heats,

378
00:27:35,237 --> 00:27:38,554
then first in the main round,
and he just kept climbing.

379
00:27:38,554 --> 00:27:42,329
When a sport no one expected anything from
keeps taking first place,

380
00:27:42,329 --> 00:27:44,727
I wonder if you know that thrill.

381
00:27:45,457 --> 00:27:48,625
Why would I know a thrill like that?

382
00:27:48,625 --> 00:27:52,792
My parents sat in front of the TV at dawn
with bloodshot eyes.

383
00:27:52,792 --> 00:27:56,800
And it was swimming, not even soccer.
I'd never seen them watch like that.

384
00:27:56,800 --> 00:28:02,332
But Cho Jae Jin made it to the final
and then withdrew.

385
00:28:02,332 --> 00:28:06,013
Even though his record so far was enough
to win easily.

386
00:28:09,565 --> 00:28:11,117
Sit down for a second.

387
00:28:11,117 --> 00:28:12,735
Sit, kid.

388
00:28:17,046 --> 00:28:21,408
People back then said
that Cho Jae Jin had been doping,

389
00:28:21,408 --> 00:28:24,065
and ran before a doping test could catch him.

390
00:28:25,621 --> 00:28:30,792
He really did retire like that,
so the truth never came out.

391
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:35,519
Then, years later, I came to this school
as the swim team coach.

392
00:28:35,519 --> 00:28:40,387
And our vice principal said to me,
"You know Cho Jae Jin, don't you?

393
00:28:40,387 --> 00:28:44,097
His son is on our school's swim team."

394
00:28:44,097 --> 00:28:46,183
- So?
- What do you mean, "so"?

395
00:28:46,183 --> 00:28:47,559
So I asked him.

396
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:51,284
"Sir, so what's Cho Jae Jin doing now?"

397
00:28:51,284 --> 00:28:55,025
"If his son's on the swim team,
is he coaching or something?"

398
00:28:55,025 --> 00:28:57,188
"No. He's making soy sauce."

399
00:28:57,188 --> 00:28:58,667
Our soy sauce is delicious.

400
00:28:58,667 --> 00:28:59,833
Ever tried it?

401
00:28:59,833 --> 00:29:01,146
Chestnut rice wine too, right?

402
00:29:01,146 --> 00:29:03,302
That's good, too. It sells out nationwide.

403
00:29:03,302 --> 00:29:05,577
Want me to steal you one?

404
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:09,539
Still, what made me feel okay was
that his son was on our swim team.

405
00:29:09,539 --> 00:29:13,094
He wouldn't go off making soy sauce
and chestnut rice wine.

406
00:29:13,094 --> 00:29:14,461
So I want you to compete--

407
00:29:14,461 --> 00:29:16,628
No, I'm going to make it.

408
00:29:16,628 --> 00:29:19,500
Tastier, sweeter and nuttier than my dad's.

409
00:29:19,500 --> 00:29:21,602
Just shut up.

410
00:29:22,759 --> 00:29:24,721
Let me be honest.

411
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:26,306
I've never come in first.

412
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:28,183
So I don't know how winners feel.

413
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:31,647
But I've made plenty of winners.

414
00:29:31,647 --> 00:29:35,524
That feels insanely good, too.

415
00:29:35,524 --> 00:29:39,138
So how must it feel to actually win?

416
00:29:40,572 --> 00:29:42,606
Not my problem.

417
00:29:47,287 --> 00:29:50,031
Cho Yu Gyeom, you really
plan to keep living like this?

418
00:29:50,031 --> 00:29:51,526
Like your dad?

419
00:29:53,479 --> 00:29:54,703
Sir.

420
00:29:55,366 --> 00:29:57,650
I have three older sisters.

421
00:29:57,650 --> 00:29:58,656
Are they pretty?

422
00:29:59,672 --> 00:30:01,462
None of them went to college.

423
00:30:01,462 --> 00:30:03,997
No, they couldn't.

424
00:30:04,675 --> 00:30:05,713
Why?

425
00:30:06,866 --> 00:30:08,332
They're girls.

426
00:30:12,813 --> 00:30:15,870
That's the kind of family I have, sir.
What do you expect?

427
00:30:15,870 --> 00:30:17,774
Hey, wait.

428
00:30:17,774 --> 00:30:22,568
I wasn't done talking, and he just walks off.
He could at least introduce me.

429
00:30:26,926 --> 00:30:29,971
Sorry, Jeong Uk. Do one more lap.

430
00:30:29,971 --> 00:30:31,286
I didn't get your time.

431
00:30:31,286 --> 00:30:32,634
I'm done.

432
00:30:32,634 --> 00:30:33,652
Okay, go.

433
00:30:35,282 --> 00:30:38,590
Do what I say, you punk. Hurry up and go.

434
00:30:52,017 --> 00:30:54,888
The person you're calling isn't answering...

435
00:30:54,888 --> 00:30:56,415
Cho Yu Gyeom!

436
00:31:05,101 --> 00:31:09,575
Um, hey. You...

437
00:31:09,575 --> 00:31:11,538
So...

438
00:31:11,538 --> 00:31:14,115
Um. Me? So?

439
00:31:14,115 --> 00:31:15,382
What is it?

440
00:31:15,382 --> 00:31:18,460
I heard you broke up with Sung Sae Ryeong.

441
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:20,434
So what?

442
00:31:22,547 --> 00:31:23,921
Then maybe I could--

443
00:31:23,921 --> 00:31:25,928
Hey! Cho Yu Gyeom!

444
00:31:25,928 --> 00:31:28,347
Um, over there...

445
00:31:28,347 --> 00:31:30,869
S-Sung Sae Ryeong.

446
00:31:34,898 --> 00:31:37,439
Oh, Sae Ryeong. What's up?

447
00:31:37,439 --> 00:31:40,638
Phew, or is it just me?

448
00:31:40,638 --> 00:31:42,594
The weather's...

449
00:31:44,068 --> 00:31:45,391
hot.

450
00:31:47,322 --> 00:31:50,876
I told you I'd break up with you, right?
That I could do that.

451
00:31:50,876 --> 00:31:53,370
But I asked you not to tell anyone for now.

452
00:31:53,370 --> 00:31:56,322
I said never tell!

453
00:31:56,322 --> 00:31:59,382
We broke up. Why can't I say that?

454
00:31:59,382 --> 00:32:01,626
Shit, because I'm fucked!

455
00:32:01,626 --> 00:32:05,144
No, I'm already fucked, damn it.

456
00:32:05,144 --> 00:32:06,276
Cho Yu Gyeom.

457
00:32:06,276 --> 00:32:11,200
Everyone knows we broke up. If I walk out
of this bathroom, they're all ready to

458
00:32:12,401 --> 00:32:15,549
throw shit at me. Do you get it?

459
00:32:16,381 --> 00:32:17,633
So?

460
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:20,711
So did they get you?

461
00:32:21,481 --> 00:32:22,959
What? Hey.

462
00:32:22,959 --> 00:32:24,862
No one's gotten you yet, Sae Ryeong.

463
00:32:24,862 --> 00:32:26,444
What do you mean, Yu Gyeom?

464
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:30,275
Even if they did, don't call me.

465
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:34,202
Cho Yu Gyeom! Cho Yu--

466
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:37,641
What? Did you really break up?

467
00:33:02,189 --> 00:33:04,882
Sir, please follow that car. Hurry.

468
00:33:04,882 --> 00:33:07,148
What if we get caught like this?

469
00:33:07,148 --> 00:33:09,602
I told you not to worry about that.

470
00:33:09,602 --> 00:33:11,323
I'm still nervous about Sae Ryeong.

471
00:33:11,323 --> 00:33:13,521
I said forget it.

472
00:33:30,167 --> 00:33:32,455
- Hey.
- What?

473
00:33:33,162 --> 00:33:35,242
I'm shaking. I don't think I can go.

474
00:33:35,242 --> 00:33:37,974
Hold on. It's almost party time.

475
00:33:37,974 --> 00:33:39,100
Ryu Si Yeon, you're filming, right?

476
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:40,936
Yeah. I'm filming.

477
00:33:40,936 --> 00:33:44,606
But look. Anyone can tell
there's no mansion out here.

478
00:33:44,606 --> 00:33:47,865
Even when Sae Ryeong lies,
she gets caught right away.

479
00:33:47,865 --> 00:33:49,678
- Kim Jin Mi.
- What?

480
00:33:51,655 --> 00:33:54,262
Holy shit, that's insane.

481
00:33:54,262 --> 00:33:56,137
Kim Jin Mi.

482
00:33:56,137 --> 00:33:57,327
Seriously.

483
00:33:57,327 --> 00:33:59,346
No way.

484
00:33:59,346 --> 00:34:01,873
Hey, Kim Jin Mi!

485
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:03,527
Hey!

486
00:34:09,542 --> 00:34:13,426
Kim Jin Mi, what are you doing?

487
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:15,662
She actually lives here.

488
00:34:15,662 --> 00:34:17,512
No, no way.

489
00:34:17,512 --> 00:34:19,933
This can't be real. No.

490
00:34:19,933 --> 00:34:23,221
See? I told you Sae Ryeong was off.

491
00:34:23,221 --> 00:34:26,091
How do you swing and miss this badly?

492
00:34:27,042 --> 00:34:28,912
No. This can't be.

493
00:34:28,912 --> 00:34:31,111
This is really...

494
00:34:31,111 --> 00:34:34,844
Wait here a minute. I'll get you a cold drink.

495
00:34:34,844 --> 00:34:35,913
Okay.

496
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:44,679
Let's just go.

497
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:47,962
If Sae Ryeong sees us, we're so screwed.

498
00:34:47,962 --> 00:34:49,172
Yeah. Let's hurry up.

499
00:34:51,125 --> 00:34:52,804
What are you doing? Come on!

500
00:34:52,804 --> 00:34:55,575
Leave her. She's fucking dying to get caught.

501
00:34:55,575 --> 00:34:58,888
She must want to get fucking caught
and torn to shreds.

502
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:00,342
Ugh, seriously.

503
00:35:06,570 --> 00:35:07,605
Thank you.

504
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:10,859
So what brings you here today?
It's not your usual day.

505
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:13,648
I can't make it tomorrow, so I came today.

506
00:35:13,648 --> 00:35:16,817
Is that so? What a good girl.

507
00:35:21,494 --> 00:35:24,414
Kim Jin Mi's blunder was epic.

508
00:35:24,414 --> 00:35:30,339
If Sung Sae Ryeong fucking finds out,
I'll wreck you first.

509
00:35:30,339 --> 00:35:34,415
Sae Ryeong and I are going
to the department store tomorrow.

510
00:35:34,415 --> 00:35:35,667
Whatever.

511
00:35:35,667 --> 00:35:37,042
Let her go.

512
00:35:37,042 --> 00:35:41,060
Guess she'll grovel
and beg Sae Ryeong for forgiveness.

513
00:35:41,060 --> 00:35:44,520
If you ask me, it's not over with
Cho Yu Gyeom either.

514
00:35:44,520 --> 00:35:47,814
Shit, if Cho Yu Gyeom found out...

515
00:35:47,814 --> 00:35:51,928
Her bag is fake. I'll go and prove it.

516
00:35:51,928 --> 00:35:54,625
Awesome, epic, let it go.

517
00:36:46,874 --> 00:36:49,199
- Boo!
- Oh, you scared me!

518
00:36:52,134 --> 00:36:54,401
How are you so good at swimming?

519
00:36:56,423 --> 00:36:58,095
Do you have air conditioning at home?

520
00:36:58,095 --> 00:37:00,504
Yeah, of course.

521
00:37:01,374 --> 00:37:02,903
We don't have one.

522
00:37:03,849 --> 00:37:05,140
Really?

523
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:06,310
Yeah.

524
00:37:07,214 --> 00:37:10,480
No AC, and no computer either.

525
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:12,522
The only TV is in my grandfather's room.

526
00:37:12,522 --> 00:37:16,099
And we can't even get internet.

527
00:37:17,022 --> 00:37:18,600
No way.

528
00:37:19,434 --> 00:37:21,596
So I started swimming.

529
00:37:22,284 --> 00:37:24,297
Summers are so hot.

530
00:37:25,194 --> 00:37:27,452
At least the sea is cool.

531
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:31,289
That's how I got good at it.

532
00:37:34,335 --> 00:37:36,379
So it's a God-given gift?

533
00:37:36,379 --> 00:37:40,134
No, I said I got good because it's so hot.

534
00:37:40,134 --> 00:37:43,386
Doing it every day doesn't
necessarily make it a talent.

535
00:37:43,386 --> 00:37:47,110
I study every day, and I'm still bad at it.

536
00:37:49,994 --> 00:37:53,828
Didn't your parents say anything
when you left today?

537
00:37:56,254 --> 00:37:57,728
Kim Ha Yeon!

538
00:37:58,354 --> 00:37:59,915
Going out again?

539
00:38:03,566 --> 00:38:05,512
Look at you!

540
00:38:05,512 --> 00:38:07,412
You still haven't come to your senses.

541
00:38:07,412 --> 00:38:09,500
Not one bit.

542
00:38:09,500 --> 00:38:14,516
Your brother's torn ear hasn't even healed yet.

543
00:38:15,629 --> 00:38:19,401
Mom, I have a boyfriend.

544
00:38:21,334 --> 00:38:22,511
What?

545
00:38:27,054 --> 00:38:28,285
So?

546
00:38:29,017 --> 00:38:31,300
I'm going on a date for a bit.

547
00:38:35,074 --> 00:38:36,564
What?

548
00:38:36,564 --> 00:38:40,025
A-A date?

549
00:38:40,985 --> 00:38:45,532
Mom, I'll never amount to anything,
no matter how hard I try.

550
00:38:45,532 --> 00:38:49,200
So I decided to be happy, at least today.

551
00:38:49,200 --> 00:38:51,095
So I'm going on a date.

552
00:38:51,095 --> 00:38:54,004
I won't be too late. See you later.

553
00:38:56,209 --> 00:38:59,965
Hey! Kim Ha Yeon!

554
00:38:59,965 --> 00:39:01,713
Seriously.

555
00:39:02,632 --> 00:39:06,012
What's gotten into her?

556
00:39:06,012 --> 00:39:07,999
Why is she acting like that?

557
00:39:08,849 --> 00:39:10,545
Ugh, seriously.

558
00:39:11,432 --> 00:39:16,398
- Seriously.
- My mom isn't someone who changes easily.

559
00:39:17,374 --> 00:39:19,464
So I decided to change.

560
00:39:21,354 --> 00:39:23,971
That's a good idea.

561
00:39:23,971 --> 00:39:26,216
Cool, right?

562
00:39:30,234 --> 00:39:31,721
Oh, right.

563
00:39:31,721 --> 00:39:33,081
Your mom...

564
00:39:33,081 --> 00:39:34,085
Yeah.

565
00:39:39,922 --> 00:39:41,154
Yeah. I'm going.

566
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:46,391
Yu Gyeom!

567
00:39:47,387 --> 00:39:48,804
Are you okay?

568
00:39:48,804 --> 00:39:51,748
I looked everywhere for you.

569
00:39:55,062 --> 00:39:57,029
She was really pretty.

570
00:40:01,693 --> 00:40:03,113
In my family,

571
00:40:04,960 --> 00:40:06,525
only Mom is mine.

572
00:40:08,742 --> 00:40:10,333
Lucky you,

573
00:40:11,353 --> 00:40:13,308
that Mom is yours.

574
00:40:18,134 --> 00:40:19,531
Lucky you, too,

575
00:40:23,340 --> 00:40:24,891
that I'm yours.

576
00:40:25,926 --> 00:40:27,490
What?

577
00:40:30,354 --> 00:40:31,929
What did you say?

578
00:40:31,929 --> 00:40:34,429
Say it louder.

579
00:40:34,429 --> 00:40:35,725
It's nothing.

580
00:40:35,725 --> 00:40:38,853
Say it louder.

581
00:40:38,853 --> 00:40:40,888
What?

582
00:40:40,888 --> 00:40:43,193
- Say it louder.
- No, stop it.

583
00:40:43,193 --> 00:40:44,930
I'm really hurt.

584
00:40:44,930 --> 00:40:46,778
Hurt? That was hard for me to say.

585
00:40:46,778 --> 00:40:48,782
- I want to hear more.
- I'm sorry.

586
00:40:48,782 --> 00:40:50,684
Tell me more. More.

587
00:40:55,918 --> 00:40:58,965
[Death and time]
[What is death?]

588
00:41:00,918 --> 00:41:02,757
[The sorrow of death]
[The house of death]

589
00:41:07,254 --> 00:41:09,842
Please check your first-semester grades.

590
00:41:09,842 --> 00:41:11,763
Who was top of the class?

591
00:41:11,763 --> 00:41:12,845
Isn't it Kim Jung Yeon?

592
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:14,376
No, no. Oh Ji Eun.

593
00:41:14,376 --> 00:41:18,833
Yeah. Getting good grades without once
opening a book was honestly ridiculous.

594
00:41:20,189 --> 00:41:22,812
Seems a bit human, finally.

595
00:41:24,687 --> 00:41:27,172
What's it to you guys?

596
00:41:33,542 --> 00:41:35,679
[Sign language tutoring]

597
00:41:37,780 --> 00:41:39,554
What are you doing? Still up?

598
00:41:39,554 --> 00:41:41,554
Mom, I'm going to sleep.

599
00:41:42,834 --> 00:41:44,671
Good night, Mom.

600
00:41:44,671 --> 00:41:49,728
By the way, what did you and that boy
talk about yesterday?

601
00:41:51,780 --> 00:41:53,594
No.

602
00:41:53,594 --> 00:41:55,225
Nothing.

603
00:41:55,225 --> 00:41:56,688
Don't tell me...

604
00:41:58,653 --> 00:42:02,218
You haven't fallen for him already, have you?

605
00:42:02,218 --> 00:42:05,690
No. That's not it. No.

606
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:09,473
Sam Hee, your face says it all.

607
00:42:09,473 --> 00:42:11,500
No, Mom. It's not like that.

608
00:42:11,500 --> 00:42:18,327
He wants me to teach him sign language,
so I got a little flustered.

609
00:42:18,327 --> 00:42:19,378
I really mean it.

610
00:42:19,378 --> 00:42:23,726
Really? Then you can teach him.

611
00:42:23,726 --> 00:42:28,004
But you can just learn sign language
from videos or something, so...

612
00:42:28,004 --> 00:42:31,027
But he asked you to teach him, right?

613
00:42:31,027 --> 00:42:36,101
So you can teach him and earn pocket money,

614
00:42:37,547 --> 00:42:40,335
and spend time with someone you like.

615
00:42:41,603 --> 00:42:43,663
- Two birds with one stone.
- No, Mom.

616
00:42:43,663 --> 00:42:46,137
No, no. I really don't like him.

617
00:42:46,137 --> 00:42:48,775
Come on, I only met him yesterday.

618
00:42:48,775 --> 00:42:53,236
It was just such a sudden offer
that I got flustered.

619
00:42:56,030 --> 00:42:58,305
Right. You don't like him.

620
00:42:58,305 --> 00:42:59,641
Yet.

621
00:42:59,641 --> 00:43:03,726
Mom, it's really not like that.

622
00:43:03,726 --> 00:43:07,839
Okay, since you don't like him,
just give it a try.

623
00:43:07,839 --> 00:43:14,590
It's bothered me, too, seeing you stuck
in the kitchen at such a pretty age.

624
00:43:14,590 --> 00:43:18,638
Use teaching him as an excuse
to get out a bit, okay?

625
00:43:18,638 --> 00:43:22,679
Eat something tasty, see something fun.

626
00:43:22,679 --> 00:43:23,937
Wouldn't that be nice?

627
00:43:23,937 --> 00:43:27,013
Grandpa does all that for me anyway.

628
00:43:28,807 --> 00:43:30,115
True.

629
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:36,783
But Grandpa doesn't give you butterflies.
Am I right?

630
00:43:36,783 --> 00:43:39,266
It's really not like that, Mom.

631
00:43:39,266 --> 00:43:44,109
Do you have to like someone to get butterflies?
Meeting someone new does it too.

632
00:43:44,109 --> 00:43:47,167
Why were you staring at your phone all day?

633
00:43:47,167 --> 00:43:49,459
It's not him. It's my other friends.

634
00:43:49,459 --> 00:43:52,117
What are you looking at, Mom?

635
00:44:02,865 --> 00:44:05,707
I'm sorry, honey.

636
00:44:06,672 --> 00:44:09,215
I'm sorry.

637
00:44:10,186 --> 00:44:14,409
I take back what I said,

638
00:44:16,653 --> 00:44:21,706
that you'll never amount to anything,
no matter how hard you try.

639
00:44:21,706 --> 00:44:23,701
I'm sorry, sweetheart.

640
00:44:26,122 --> 00:44:29,917
So can you please stop this now?

641
00:44:29,917 --> 00:44:32,095
I'm not asking for much.

642
00:44:32,095 --> 00:44:34,338
Just go back to how things were.

643
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:37,508
Let's just live the way we used to.

644
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:39,513
Okay, Ha Yeon?

645
00:44:39,513 --> 00:44:41,095
Can you do that for me?

646
00:44:41,095 --> 00:44:44,018
I'll never make that mistake...

647
00:44:46,853 --> 00:44:48,221
Wait right there.

648
00:44:48,221 --> 00:44:50,423
I'm not done talking.

649
00:44:51,206 --> 00:44:52,866
Yes, hello?

650
00:44:56,613 --> 00:45:01,120
Yes, what's this about?

651
00:45:01,706 --> 00:45:04,020
Yes.

652
00:45:15,946 --> 00:45:17,471
What?

653
00:45:17,471 --> 00:45:18,932
You think this is funny?

654
00:45:19,720 --> 00:45:22,346
No, it's not funny.

655
00:45:22,346 --> 00:45:23,818
Then why are you laughing?

656
00:45:24,919 --> 00:45:26,811
Because you're funny.

657
00:45:27,426 --> 00:45:28,623
Me?

658
00:45:30,159 --> 00:45:34,179
"Mom, I have a boyfriend."

659
00:45:34,179 --> 00:45:36,361
Seriously.

660
00:45:36,361 --> 00:45:37,869
Stop it.

661
00:45:38,655 --> 00:45:42,798
"Mom, I'm going out on a date for a bit."

662
00:45:42,798 --> 00:45:44,423
I said stop it.

663
00:45:44,423 --> 00:45:47,870
"Mom, I've decided to live my own life."

664
00:45:47,870 --> 00:45:49,262
So annoying.

665
00:45:49,262 --> 00:45:50,417
"So annoying."

666
00:45:50,417 --> 00:45:53,067
Are you crazy? Seriously, stop.

667
00:45:54,043 --> 00:45:56,131
- Stop it. I mean it.
- Nice.

668
00:45:56,131 --> 00:46:00,620
I said stop! What's so nice about it?
Hurry up and eat. Seriously.

669
00:46:02,596 --> 00:46:04,746
Stop staring at me. Seriously.

670
00:46:04,746 --> 00:46:08,696
Do that one more time and I'll hit you.
I mean it. I really mean it.

671
00:46:23,739 --> 00:46:27,532
Sae Ryeong, you remember we're going to
the department store today, right?

672
00:46:27,532 --> 00:46:29,829
Forget it. I'll just throw the bag out.

673
00:46:29,829 --> 00:46:32,542
Why throw away something so expensive?

674
00:46:32,542 --> 00:46:36,004
Then just give it to me. I'll use it.

675
00:46:36,004 --> 00:46:37,172
What are you doing?

676
00:46:37,172 --> 00:46:39,630
If you can't give it away, sell it to me.

677
00:46:39,630 --> 00:46:42,591
I can take it to the store and fix it.

678
00:46:42,591 --> 00:46:43,646
How much was it?

679
00:46:43,646 --> 00:46:45,906
- This was about--
- Okay, fine.

680
00:46:47,746 --> 00:46:48,804
You'll sell it to me?

681
00:46:48,804 --> 00:46:52,199
No, I said let's go to the department store.

682
00:46:53,846 --> 00:46:54,946
Okay, then later--

683
00:46:54,946 --> 00:46:56,409
Why wait until later?

684
00:46:56,409 --> 00:46:58,286
If we're going, go now.

685
00:46:58,286 --> 00:46:59,542
Class is about to--

686
00:46:59,542 --> 00:47:02,083
Since when do we care about
supplementary class?

687
00:47:02,083 --> 00:47:03,792
I'm leaving now.

688
00:47:03,792 --> 00:47:05,387
Come if you want.

689
00:47:05,387 --> 00:47:06,681
If not, whatever.

690
00:47:08,019 --> 00:47:09,993
Sae Ryeong, wait for me.

691
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:35,221
This one's new for fall and winter.

692
00:47:35,221 --> 00:47:37,605
Only two have come into Korea.

693
00:47:37,605 --> 00:47:40,000
And this one is a staple of our store.

694
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:44,677
It's the one our customers ask for most,
and it just came in this morning.

695
00:47:46,086 --> 00:47:47,471
Can I try this one?

696
00:47:47,471 --> 00:47:49,460
Of course.

697
00:47:58,086 --> 00:48:00,179
It looks so good on you.

698
00:48:04,212 --> 00:48:06,970
Sae Ryeong, I said we'd get your bag fixed.

699
00:48:06,970 --> 00:48:09,865
I'm just going to buy a new one.

700
00:48:13,226 --> 00:48:15,666
I don't have that kind of money.

701
00:48:15,666 --> 00:48:17,156
I know.

702
00:48:17,156 --> 00:48:18,591
Someone like you wouldn't.

703
00:48:19,666 --> 00:48:20,763
How much is this?

704
00:48:20,763 --> 00:48:23,728
It's 6,822,000 won.

705
00:48:24,986 --> 00:48:26,886
- I'll take it.
- Shall I ring it up?

706
00:48:26,886 --> 00:48:28,407
Yes, please.

707
00:48:31,046 --> 00:48:32,262
Then how much should I...

708
00:48:32,262 --> 00:48:33,798
Forget it.

709
00:48:33,798 --> 00:48:35,999
I'm letting you off the hook.

710
00:48:35,999 --> 00:48:37,313
What did you say?

711
00:48:38,168 --> 00:48:39,458
Installments?

712
00:48:39,458 --> 00:48:40,491
In full.

713
00:48:40,491 --> 00:48:42,081
Okay.

714
00:48:42,081 --> 00:48:44,338
I'm the one letting you off the hook.

715
00:48:44,338 --> 00:48:49,041
So I hope you'll keep your head down
in your place like always.

716
00:48:50,977 --> 00:48:53,886
Ma'am, do you have anything else?

717
00:48:56,270 --> 00:49:01,853
Kim Jin Mi, you've got it all wrong.
She's buying it. And paying in full.

718
00:49:06,238 --> 00:49:08,471
She'll buy it and return it for sure.

719
00:49:08,471 --> 00:49:11,579
She'll take it home and return it as is.

720
00:49:15,251 --> 00:49:18,747
- Ma'am, just take off all the tags.
- Pardon?

721
00:49:18,747 --> 00:49:21,750
Then it'll be hard to exchange or refund it.

722
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:23,179
I don't do that.

723
00:49:23,179 --> 00:49:25,143
I'd rather buy a new one.

724
00:49:28,042 --> 00:49:29,429
What?

725
00:49:29,429 --> 00:49:31,584
What's with that look?

726
00:49:31,584 --> 00:49:33,542
Nothing, Sae Ryeong.

727
00:49:33,542 --> 00:49:36,348
You guys, is there anything you want?

728
00:49:36,348 --> 00:49:38,471
Should I buy you something while we're here?

729
00:49:38,471 --> 00:49:40,177
Really?

730
00:49:40,177 --> 00:49:43,257
That'd be awesome.

731
00:49:45,149 --> 00:49:48,473
You should just admit it too.

732
00:49:48,473 --> 00:49:52,155
Sae Ryeong won't crumble over
whatever you say or do.

733
00:49:56,651 --> 00:49:58,679
Isn't this color pretty?

734
00:49:58,679 --> 00:50:00,209
Yeah, it suits you.

735
00:50:04,017 --> 00:50:06,554
Kim Jin Mi, I heard you blew it again?

736
00:50:06,554 --> 00:50:08,631
How long can you keep up the fucking lies?

737
00:50:08,631 --> 00:50:11,342
See you at school tomorrow.

738
00:50:11,342 --> 00:50:15,429
Look. The more you act up,
the deeper you dig your own hole.

739
00:50:15,429 --> 00:50:17,890
Was I the only one who hated Sae Ryeong?

740
00:50:17,890 --> 00:50:20,145
You all hated her guts, too.

741
00:50:20,145 --> 00:50:23,863
But Jin Mi, I'm saying now's not the moment.

742
00:50:24,542 --> 00:50:27,325
And maybe that moment will never come.

743
00:50:28,108 --> 00:50:30,792
Sae Ryeong has power.

744
00:50:30,792 --> 00:50:33,500
So just keep your head down,
like Sae Ryeong said.

745
00:50:33,500 --> 00:50:36,881
You know what happens if you cross the queen.

746
00:50:40,626 --> 00:50:42,471
Anyway, this is so pretty.

747
00:50:42,471 --> 00:50:44,167
Luxury brands are different, right?

748
00:50:44,167 --> 00:50:45,512
So you're cool-toned?

749
00:50:45,512 --> 00:50:46,956
How'd you know?

750
00:50:48,250 --> 00:50:49,510
Ha Yeon.

751
00:50:57,991 --> 00:50:59,195
Want to ride with me?

752
00:51:03,155 --> 00:51:06,900
No. I'll just walk.

753
00:51:06,900 --> 00:51:08,574
Come on, ride with me.

754
00:51:12,459 --> 00:51:14,068
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

755
00:51:15,458 --> 00:51:16,809
I'll come back.

756
00:51:18,751 --> 00:51:20,455
- Should I go?
- Yeah.

757
00:51:20,455 --> 00:51:21,888
Okay, I'm going.

758
00:51:21,888 --> 00:51:22,940
See you later.

759
00:51:22,940 --> 00:51:24,101
Yeah.

760
00:51:26,118 --> 00:51:28,938
- What are you doing? Go.
- It won't go forward.

761
00:51:28,938 --> 00:51:31,392
Go, hurry. Go.

762
00:51:33,518 --> 00:51:35,351
- See you.
- Yeah.

763
00:51:44,605 --> 00:51:47,095
Yeah. Heel down, then toe.

764
00:51:47,095 --> 00:51:50,551
Heel down, then toe. Faster.

765
00:51:51,275 --> 00:51:53,012
Why can't you get it?

766
00:51:53,012 --> 00:51:54,069
Isn't this right?

767
00:51:54,069 --> 00:51:55,584
- Got it.
- I said heel, toe.

768
00:51:55,584 --> 00:51:58,659
- Got it.
- Heel, toe. You have to be quick.

769
00:52:03,484 --> 00:52:04,670
Sae Ryeong.

770
00:52:06,168 --> 00:52:07,707
Sae Ryeong!

771
00:52:09,350 --> 00:52:10,961
Where's Kim Jin Mi?

772
00:52:10,961 --> 00:52:12,238
No idea.

773
00:52:12,238 --> 00:52:15,799
Sae Ryeong, the tint you got me is so pretty.

774
00:52:15,799 --> 00:52:18,375
- Oh, really?
- I'm wearing it again today.

775
00:52:18,375 --> 00:52:20,429
What? I'm wearing it, too.

776
00:52:20,429 --> 00:52:22,029
Why are you copying me?

777
00:52:22,948 --> 00:52:27,042
Sae Ryeong, what does your grandpa do?

778
00:52:27,042 --> 00:52:28,699
My grandpa?

779
00:52:29,358 --> 00:52:31,460
They've both passed away.

780
00:52:32,167 --> 00:52:33,959
- Really?
- Yeah.

781
00:52:33,959 --> 00:52:37,738
There's an old lady at my house,
but she works for us.

782
00:52:37,738 --> 00:52:41,617
My mom says I can never be alone with a man,
even an old grandpa.

783
00:52:41,617 --> 00:52:44,792
You know, political families are conservative.

784
00:52:55,724 --> 00:52:57,929
Who are you?

785
00:52:57,929 --> 00:53:00,037
Hello, sir.

786
00:53:09,186 --> 00:53:11,855
Got a haircut, and...

787
00:53:11,855 --> 00:53:16,100
Seriously, it's insane. Where is it? I saw it.

788
00:53:16,100 --> 00:53:17,179
What is it? Let me see.

789
00:53:17,179 --> 00:53:19,954
It's fucking hilarious. Look.

790
00:53:25,709 --> 00:53:27,542
Going to the bathroom real quick.

791
00:53:27,542 --> 00:53:29,442
Me too. I'll come with you.

792
00:53:44,878 --> 00:53:48,137
You mean that girl Sae Ryeong, right?

793
00:53:48,137 --> 00:53:49,598
Yes.

794
00:53:49,598 --> 00:53:53,831
She's the one who mops our villa's floors.

795
00:53:53,831 --> 00:53:55,533
Mopping the floors?

796
00:53:56,191 --> 00:54:01,865
Well, she lives at the foot of that mountain
with her grandma.

797
00:54:01,865 --> 00:54:04,655
She's such a good kid.

798
00:54:05,451 --> 00:54:11,915
She comes by our villa now and then
to mop and clean for me.

799
00:54:11,915 --> 00:54:15,816
She can see it's hard for me
to manage the villa alone.

800
00:54:15,816 --> 00:54:18,252
She helps me out so much.

801
00:54:18,967 --> 00:54:21,678
So you're not related to Sae Ryeong, sir?

802
00:54:21,678 --> 00:54:24,119
- That's insane.
- It was all a big lie?

803
00:54:24,119 --> 00:54:25,724
Complete strangers.

804
00:54:25,724 --> 00:54:29,390
But she works so hard to help me out.

805
00:54:30,979 --> 00:54:32,462
Whose villa is it?

806
00:54:32,462 --> 00:54:34,409
- That's insane.
- Shh.

807
00:54:35,651 --> 00:54:38,734
Did you guys see?

808
00:54:38,734 --> 00:54:40,152
We're watching right now.

809
00:54:40,152 --> 00:54:41,574
Is it Sae Ryeong's father?

810
00:54:41,574 --> 00:54:43,221
What?

811
00:54:43,221 --> 00:54:46,158
I told you, she lives down that mountain
with her grandma.

812
00:54:46,158 --> 00:54:49,126
She has a really hard life.

813
00:55:10,641 --> 00:55:15,792
Sung Sae Ryeong, I still want to give you
at least a little money.

814
00:55:15,792 --> 00:55:18,126
To pay for that bag, I mean.

815
00:55:18,126 --> 00:55:21,395
So, can you come to the rooftop for a sec?

816
00:55:37,228 --> 00:55:38,651
So?

817
00:55:39,488 --> 00:55:41,752
So what am I supposed to do?

818
00:55:41,752 --> 00:55:44,804
Sae Ryeong asked to talk for a minute.

819
00:55:45,428 --> 00:55:46,729
And you...

820
00:55:47,427 --> 00:55:48,901
believe that?

821
00:55:53,048 --> 00:55:54,109
Yeah.

822
00:55:55,628 --> 00:55:59,211
Because when I'm with you,
I'm not scared at all.

823
00:56:01,653 --> 00:56:03,520
So you want me to go with you?

824
00:56:06,188 --> 00:56:08,008
Could you do that?

825
00:56:09,968 --> 00:56:11,472
Okay, let's go.

826
00:56:22,212 --> 00:56:23,387
What is this?

827
00:56:23,387 --> 00:56:26,133
Mop water from the bathroom. What else?

828
00:56:26,133 --> 00:56:32,164
Even if it's out that Sae Ryeong's broke,
don't you think you're going too far?

829
00:56:32,164 --> 00:56:34,558
Seo Gyeong, was it ninth grade for you?

830
00:56:34,558 --> 00:56:38,168
That bald spot from one wrong word
to Cho Yu Gyeom.

831
00:56:38,168 --> 00:56:40,776
You still have it, don't you?

832
00:56:40,776 --> 00:56:44,528
Somewhere on the back of your head,
like an idiot.

833
00:56:45,751 --> 00:56:47,848
You guys are so nice.

834
00:56:47,848 --> 00:56:51,003
Is it because you're country kids?
How are you so nice?

835
00:56:54,348 --> 00:56:58,814
Guys, that bitch Sung Sae Ryeong
is nothing now.

836
00:56:59,441 --> 00:57:02,628
No Cho Yu Gyeom going crazy
when someone touches her,

837
00:57:02,628 --> 00:57:07,568
and no parents rushing over to raise hell.
Fuck, she never had any to begin with.

838
00:57:07,568 --> 00:57:11,845
Her grandma can't even talk.
She can't hear, either. Isn't that crazy?

839
00:57:11,845 --> 00:57:14,042
So what can we do now?

840
00:57:14,042 --> 00:57:15,679
Like she did to us...

841
00:57:20,941 --> 00:57:22,958
I'm on my way.

842
00:57:24,236 --> 00:57:27,491
We have to pay her back, don't we?

843
00:57:40,248 --> 00:57:45,039
What if I had just died back then?

844
00:57:49,621 --> 00:57:51,759
Would Yu Gyeom have regretted it?

845
00:57:57,769 --> 00:57:59,865
Kim Ha Yeon would go to prison.

846
00:58:15,467 --> 00:58:17,049
I'll do it.

847
00:58:31,328 --> 00:58:33,665
Wouldn't it actually be better

848
00:58:34,306 --> 00:58:36,048
with just me gone?

849
00:58:39,434 --> 00:58:41,855
Why did I survive?

850
00:58:44,054 --> 00:58:46,979
Why did I end up surviving?

851
00:59:22,563 --> 00:59:25,958
Must be fun, the way you're all laughing.

852
00:59:32,988 --> 00:59:34,174
Who was it?

853
00:59:43,728 --> 00:59:45,577
I said, who was it!

854
00:59:51,528 --> 00:59:52,684
Was it you?

855
00:59:53,288 --> 00:59:55,012
Was it you? Kim Jin Mi, answer.

856
00:59:55,012 --> 00:59:58,140
- It's not that...
- Answer me!

857
00:59:58,140 --> 01:00:01,388
Even with no dad and a mom who ran off,

858
01:00:02,281 --> 01:00:04,858
why am I so pretty and beautiful,

859
01:00:06,094 --> 01:00:09,563
when my heart is so utterly ugly?

860
01:00:11,801 --> 01:00:13,115
Goodbye.

861
01:00:14,394 --> 01:00:16,660
I couldn't be the only one to die.

862
01:00:17,428 --> 01:00:19,750
So all of us, together,

863
01:00:21,205 --> 01:00:22,495
die.
